# Worksheet

**F1 Core loop**: `game` single state object; `createRng`/`initRng` seeded, `rngFloat/rngInt/rngChoice/rngShuffle` used everywhere (no stray Math.random found); `endTurn()` executes numbered fixed-order steps 1-9. Score 2.

**F2 Map**: 8x8 grid built in `initMap` from `rngFloat`; `canBuild` checks terrain but only gates the UI button, not enforced inside `buildBuilding`; `adjacencyBonus` fields defined on BUILDINGS but never read anywhere (grep shows zero consumers) — required part missing. Score 1.

**F3 Economy**: production adds outputs in `endTurn` step 3, but `consumption` (water/power inputs) is never deducted — step 4 only logs "Power shortage" without touching `game.resources.power`. No real input→output consumption chain. Storage caps enforced (`resourceCaps` clamp + overflow log) but core chain missing. Score 1.

**F4 Population**: colonists have skill/fatigue/morale/job fields; `getProductionOutput` reads `colonist.skill` via `workers` array, but `building.workers` is never populated anywhere (no assignment code) so it's always empty; fatigue never read by any production code. Score 1.

**F5 Needs**: `endTurn` deducts food/water and lowers morale on shortage (real); but `getProductionOutput` never reads `colonist.morale`, so morale never changes output — missing required link. Score 1.

**F6 Research**: 12 nodes, `canResearch` enforces prereqs, `doResearch` deducts cost; but only `resilience_1/2` (storm damage) and `trade_tech` (caravan interval) have real code effects — the other 9 nodes' "effect" text is never implemented. Also `population_tech.prereqs` references nonexistent id `'community_programs'` (actual id is `morale_1`), causing `canResearch` to throw. Score 1.

**F7 Events**: 10 defs in `EVENT_DEFINITIONS`; selection is a uniform shuffled deck (`rngShuffle`), not weighted; 6 events offer choices with mostly differing state mutations via `applyEventEffects`; cooldown (`eventCooldown`) decremented each turn. Missing "weighted" requirement. Score 1.

**F8 Trade**: `generateCaravan` prices use `game.trade.globalSupply` and live `game.resources[res]` (demandMod); `offering.quantity` capped/limited; `trade()` handles both buy/sell, called from `renderTradePanel` buttons. Score 2.

**F9 Hazard**: `triggerAshstorm` scales severity with turn, damages buildings, reduced by `stormDamageReduction`/research flags; `getProductionOutput` reduces output by `building.damage`; but `repairBuilding` is defined and never called anywhere in any render function — dead code, repair unreachable. Score 1.

**F10 Save/load**: `saveGame` serializes full state to textarea text; `loadGame` `JSON.parse`s pasted text in try/catch, shows `alert` on bad input. Score 2.

**F11 End conditions**: win (`turn>=60 && colonists>=12`) and lose (`colonists.length===0`) both checked in `endTurn`; `renderEndScreen` computes score from population/resources/research/turn. Score 2.

**F12 UI**: tab click listener toggles `.active`+`render()`; `addLog` stores turn number, shown in `renderLogPanel`; tile `.tile-tooltip` shows terrain/building/damage; keyboard shortcuts Space/Digit1-5 wired; layout uses `auto-fit` grid & flex-wrap (dedicated `.two-column` class unused but responsiveness present elsewhere). Score 2.

**F13 Dev panel**: `runTests` has 15 real invariant checks (caps, prereqs, unique IDs, RNG reproducibility, save/load roundtrip); `runBenchmark` runs 200 headless `endTurn()` calls and prints `getGameHash()`. Score 2.

**G1**: no research node effect ever modifies `getProductionOutput`'s formula (only skill/damage read); resilience/trade_tech affect storms/caravan, not yield. Score 0.

**G2**: shortage writes to `colonist.morale` (real, in `endTurn`); but `getProductionOutput` never reads morale, so "reduced labor output" link doesn't exist. Score 1.

**G3**: `triggerAshstorm` sets `building.damage`, `getProductionOutput` applies `(1-damage*0.1)` (real pipeline); `repairBuilding` exists but has zero call sites in any render/UI code — repair/recovery unreachable. Score 2.

**G4**: `generateCaravan` price formula reads `game.resources[res]` (demandMod) each caravan; `globalSupply` itself is static/never drifts. Score 3.

**G5**: `supply_shortage` and `disease` choices each branch into different `applyEventEffects` calls that durably change `game.resources`/`game.colonists` (e.g. `removeColonist`), not just logged. Score 4.

